{{Top}}
{{Otheruses|more=Warrior}}
{{Quote|Sometimes being a good soldier means doing what you think is right.|Faro Argyus|audio=ArgyusGoodSoldier.flac|<ref name="Cloak of Darkness">{{TCW|Cloak of Darkness}}</ref>}}
[[File:Bustcollection-clone-phase1.png|thumb|right|250px|Clone troopers were soldiers in the Grand Army of the Republic who were said to represent the future of galactic warfare.]]
A '''soldier''', also referred to as a '''warrior''', was a being who fought in defense of an organization, government,<ref name="Thrawn">[[Thrawn (novel)|''Thrawn'']]</ref> or ideal.<ref name="Dissent">{{TCW|Plan of Dissent}}</ref>

==Description==
===Overview===
{{Quote|Soldiers can't choose their battles. A soldier fights for an imperfect nation, not a perfect ideal.|[[Soran Keize]]|<ref name="Alphabet Squadron (novel)">[[Alphabet Squadron (novel)|''Alphabet Squadron'']]</ref>}}
Soldiers could be trained and organized to fight as part of an [[army]] or [[militia]], whereas others served as [[Special forces|special units]].<ref name="Clone Cadets">{{TCW|Clone Cadets}}</ref> [[Infantry|Infantries]] were army branches made up of soldiers.<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> Soldiers who fought purely for [[Galactic Credit Standard|monetary]] income rather than [[Politics|political]] alignment were known as [[Mercenary|mercenaries]].<ref name="Thrawn" /> Soldiers could serve in more roles than front-line fighters, as they could be stationed at an installation<ref name="Rookies">{{TCW|Rookies (episode)}}</ref> or serve as guards.<ref name="Brain Invaders">{{TCW|Brain Invaders}}</ref>

[[File:14FDLaserCannonTeamUnitExpansion-BoxArt.png|thumb|left|250px|Soldiers of the Rebel Alliance sought to defeat the Galactic Empire despite the odds.]]
Soldiers also often fought with an ideal in mind, such as honor.<ref name="Dissent" /> In fact, the rogue [[Sith Lord]] [[Maul]] believed that every soldier was bound by honor, deeming it a weakness that could be exploited.<ref name="Shades of Reason">{{TCW|Shades of Reason}}</ref> Another ideal was hope, which was often held by the soldiers of rebel movements; the [[Rebel trooper]]s and other members of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] worked off the hope that the [[Galactic Empire]] could be destroyed.<ref name="Rogue One">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>

[[Officer]]s would serve as leaders for soldiers, fighting and commanding alongside their [[troop]]s or commanding from a more secure location.<ref name="Zillo Beast">{{TCW|The Zillo Beast}}</ref> While officers who did the latter could still win battles, soldiers often appreciated it when their superior fought in combat with them, coming to respect such [[commander]]s.<ref name="The General">{{TCW|The General (episode)}}</ref> Alternatively, officers who worked away from the frontline could anger their troops, particularly if the superior's plans resulted in the [[death]]s of many soldiers. Their soldiers could also come to mock such officers, questioning if their supposed leader lacked the fighting abilities their army possessed.<ref name="Droidography">''[[Star Wars: Droidography]]''</ref>

Indeed, [[Jedi General]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] felt that the only way to truly be a leader of soldiers was to lead from the battlefront, serving in the trenches of war alongside one's army.<ref name="501 Plus One">{{StoryCite|story=501 Plus One|book=Age of Republic Special 1}}</ref> However, [[Captain]] [[Phasma]] of the [[First Order]] [[Stormtrooper Corps (First Order)|Stormtrooper Corps]] held a different opinion, believing great leaders did not command from their soldiers' front; instead, Phasma found her troops to be patriotic fools, viewing them to merely be [[cannon]] fodder who could be sacrificed to ensure her survival and victory.<ref name="Age of Resistance">[[Age of Resistance - Captain Phasma 1|''Age of Resistance - Captain Phasma'' 1]]</ref>

===Life of a soldier===
{{Quote|Good soldiers follow orders.|A saying repeated by clone troopers under the influence of their control chip|audio=GoodSoldiersFollowOrders-TU.flac|<ref name="The Unknown">{{TCW|The Unknown}}</ref>}}
Fighting in battles that they knew they could die in,<ref name="Replacements">{{TBB|Replacements}}</ref> difficult combat made up part of the life of a soldier.<ref name="Jet Encyclopedia">{{SWE|characters|clone-commander-jet|Clone Commander Jet}}</ref> However, different soldiers had different opinions on what exactly it meant to be a good soldier; the [[treason]]ous [[Senate Commando]] [[Faro Argyus]] felt that, in order to be a good soldier, one needed to do what they thought was right, but he also believed the [[clone trooper]]s of the [[Galactic Republic]] were too conditioned to understand as such. Indeed, [[Clone Commander]] [[Gree (clone trooper)|Gree]] believed all direct orders needed to be followed and was angered by Argyus' words.<ref name="Cloak of Darkness" /> Another [[Cloning|clone]], [[Clone Captain]] [[Rex]], believed following orders upheld the honor of the Republic,<ref name="Dissent" /> but he came to change his mind during the [[Battle of Umbara]]; having seen the pain inflicted by [[Jedi General]] [[Pong Krell]], Rex came to believe it was right for soldiers to disobey orders at times and make their own decisions.<ref name="Carnage of Krell">{{TCW|Carnage of Krell}}</ref>

[[File:Tup-Control-Chip.png|thumb|right|245px|Under the control of their inhibitor chips, clone troopers were made to believe that, in order to be a good soldier, they needed to obey every order.]]
Another clone trooper, [[Advanced Recon Commando]] [[Fives]], agreed that being a loyal soldier did not mean that one needed to obey every order, saying that would mean the individual in question would be the same as a pre-programmed [[battle droid]].<ref name="Carnage of Krell" /> However, the activation of a [[behavioral modification biochip]] in their mind would force clones to think differently;<ref name="Shattered">{{TCW|Shattered}}</ref> to a clone under the influence of the chip, a good soldier was one who followed every order.<ref name="The Unknown" /><ref name="Aftermath">{{TBB|Aftermath (episode)}}</ref> In fact, when [[Elite Squad Trooper]] [[ES-01]], a [[human]] recruit brought into the [[Imperial Army]] by [[Project War-Mantle]], objected to his orders to kill civilians by saying he signed up to be a soldier and not an [[Death penalty|executioner]], [[Clone Commander]] [[Crosshair]] shot him dead, passing on the belief to the rest of his [[Elite Squad|squad]] that they needed to follow every command given.<ref name="Replacements" />

==History==
===Times of peace===
{{Quote|Talk to me when you can make the call to send our soldiers to their deaths. Better yet, talk to me when you can look someone in their eyes and watch the light leave them.|[[Jerrod Segaru]] rebukes [[Viceroy]] [[Ferrol]] during the Forever War|<ref name="Convergence">''[[The High Republic: Convergence]]''</ref>}}
[[File:BattleAtBallum-2023THR1.png|thumb|left|300px|Republic Defense Coalition troopers lived in an era of peace until the eruption of the Nihil conflict.]]
The Galactic Republic was protected for [[Standard century|centuries]] by the [[Jedi Order]] who served as [[Police officer|peacekeepers]], although they maintained that they were not soldiers.<ref name="SW:AotC">{{Film|II}}</ref> During the [[High Republic Era]], soldiers,<ref name="Light of the Jedi">''[[The High Republic: Light of the Jedi]]''</ref> such as [[Republic Defense Coalition troop]]s,<ref name="THR 2023 1">[[The High Republic (2023) 1|''The High Republic'' (2023) 1]]</ref> made up part of the [[Republic Defense Coalition]].<ref name="Light of the Jedi" /> [[Republic peacekeeping troop]]s were also sent to maintain peace in conflicted locations.<ref name="Battle of Jedha">''[[The High Republic: The Battle of Jedha]]''</ref> The Republic was also protected by the [[Judicial Forces]].<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref> The [[Galactic Senate]] on [[Coruscant]] was protected by the [[Senate Guard]]<ref name="Episode I">{{Film|I}}</ref> and its elite Senate Commandos.<ref name="Cloak of Darkness" /> Meanwhile, Republic member [[Planet|worlds]] like [[Naboo]]<ref name="Episode I" /> and [[Mon Cala]] typically had their [[Planetary defense forces|own soldiers]],<ref name="Water War">{{TCW|Water War}}</ref> such as the [[Royal Naboo Security Forces]],<ref name="Episode I" /> [[Mon Calamari Guard]] and [[Mon Calamari trooper|troopers]],<ref name="Water War" /> or [[Royal Onderon Militia]].<ref name="The Soft War">{{TCW|The Soft War}}</ref>

While the galaxy at large was at peace,<ref name="SW:AotC" /> local conflicts still erupted across the galaxy, in which local soldiers,<ref name="Convergence" /> or even Republic troops should they need to step in, took part.<ref name="THR 2023 1" /> During the High Republic Era, General [[Abediah Viess]] led a [[mercenary]] army of soldiers, who were identified as her [[Viess's army|warrior-kin]].<ref name="The Blade 2">[[The High Republic — The Blade 2|''The High Republic — The Blade'' 2]]</ref> The rival worlds of [[Eiram]] and [[E'ronoh]] both maintained militaries, which clashed against each other in a series of wars that earned the overall conflict the moniker of the "[[Eiram and E'ronoh War|Forever War]]."<ref name="Convergence" /> During the [[Nihil conflict]], a number of Galactic Republic troopers of the RDC<ref name="THR 2023 1" /> saw their first taste of real battle.<ref name="TOS1">[[The High Republic: Trail of Shadows 1|''The High Republic: Trail of Shadows'' 1]]</ref> In the late Republic Era, the government started to rely on the [[Jedi]] for peacekeeping operations more and more, giving the Judicial Forces less of a role in the Republic.<ref name="Tarkin" />

===Times of war===
====Late Republic Era====
{{Quote|The Republic is doing what it can with what it has, but the designers of the Grand Army failed to prepare for every eventuality, and in many cases we've found ourselves outnumbered or outgunned. Right now we have a finite number of clone soldiers going up against what sometimes seems an infinite number of droids.|[[Orson Callan Krennic]]|<ref name="Catalyst">''[[Catalyst: A Rogue One Novel]]''</ref>}}
[[File:TCWpromo-ClonesVsDroids.png|thumb|right|300px|The Confederacy's army of droid soldiers (left) clashed with the Republic's army of cloned infantry (right) over the course of three years.]]
With the [[First Battle of Geonosis|eruption]] of the [[Clone Wars]], the Republic formed the [[Grand Army of the Republic|Grand Army]] composed of clone [[trooper]]s,<ref name="SW:AotC" /> who were considered the future for soldiers in [[Timeline of galactic history|galactic history]].<ref name="clonetroopers">{{Databank|clone-troopers|Clone Troopers}}</ref> They fought against the [[Separatist Droid Army|Droid Army]] of the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]].<ref name="SW:AotC" /> While the Separatists notably used [[battle droid]]s instead of flesh and blood soldiers, there were occasions where organic troops were deployed,<ref name="Dark Disciple">''[[Dark Disciple]]''</ref> such as the use of [[Warrior caste (Geonosian)|Geonosian warriors]] during the [[First Battle of Geonosis|First]]<ref name="SW:AotC" /> and [[Second Battle of Geonosis|Second Battles of Geonosis]],<ref name="Landing at Point Rain">{{TCW|Landing at Point Rain}}</ref> and of [[Umbaran soldier]]s during the Battle of Umbara.<ref name="Darkness on Umbara">{{TCW|Darkness on Umbara}}</ref>

Before the war, [[Jedi Master]] [[Mace Windu]] had declared to [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] that the Jedi would never act as soldiers.<ref name="SW:AotC" /> However, the Jedi found themselves as official generals and commanders at war<ref name="Brotherhood">[[Brotherhood (novel)|''Brotherhood'']]</ref> who led clone troopers on the frontlines.<ref name="TCW film">[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars (film)|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' film]]</ref> Instead of acting in the traditional Jedi understanding of peacekeeping, young Jedi, such as [[Ahsoka Tano]], found their life dedicated to warfare just as if they were a soldier.<ref name="Shattered">{{TCW|Shattered}}</ref>

====Imperial Era====
{{Quote|The galaxy is at peace, but our work is never done. A new military comprised of our own citizens, will usher in a new era of safety and security.|[[Vice Admiral]] [[Edmon Rampart]]|<ref name="Truth and Consequences">{{TBB|Truth and Consequences}}</ref>}}
[[File:BottleneckGallery-Stormtrooper.png|thumb|left|300px|Imperial stormtroopers were the elite shock troops and later standard soldiers of the Imperial Army.]]
After the war, the new Galactic Empire used the clones as the basis for the the Imperial [[stormtrooper]]s, who served as elite soldiers and shock troops.<ref name="stormtroopers">{{Databank|stormtroopers|Stormtroopers}}</ref> The transition from clones to recruited stormtroopers was sealed via the [[Imperial Defense Recruitment Bill]], with Emperor Palpatine heralding the stormtroopers as the defining image of the galaxy's new era.<ref name="Truth and Consequences" /> The stormtroopers also began to replace the [[Imperial Army trooper|regular Imperial soldiers]].<ref name="TOG">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story The Official Guide]]''</ref> The Galactic Empire also made use of elite soldiers selected from the [[Stormtrooper Corps]] called [[death trooper]]s,<ref name="Rogue One" /> who were used as commandos<ref name="HC 80">{{HelmetCollectionCite|80|Helmets}}</ref> and to guard high-placed [[Imperial officer]]s.<ref name="Rogue One" />

Across the galaxy, isolated rebel cells would emerge that opposed the Empire with their own soldiers and starships. Born from the unification of many of those rebel cells,<ref name="Cargo">{{Rebels|Secret Cargo}}</ref> the Alliance to Restore the Republic emerged and had its own identifiable Rebel troopers,<ref name="ScenetoStats">{{AtomicMassGames|url=transmission/scene-to-stats-rebel-troopers|text=Scene to Stats: Rebel Troopers}}</ref> who were its ground forces fighting against the Empire.<ref name="Episode V">{{Film|V}}</ref> [[Grysk warrior]]s fought as soldiers for<ref name="Thrawn: Alliances">''[[Thrawn: Alliances]]''</ref> the expansionist [[Grysk Hegemony]], which attempted to make inroads into Imperial space<ref name="Thrawn: Treason">''[[Thrawn: Treason]]''</ref> and engaged the stormtroopers of Darth Vader's [[1st Legion]] during the [[Imperial–Grysk conflict]].<ref name="Thrawn: Alliances" />

===New Republic Era===
[[File:FOStormtrooperSquad-SWBC54.png|thumb|right|300px|First Order stormtroopers served as the primary infantry force of the First Order.]]
The [[New Republic]] had its own [[New Republic soldier]]s,<ref name="Bloodline">[[Bloodline (novel)|''Bloodline'']]</ref> but its decision to ignore the First Order meant the [[Resistance]] had to rely on lightly-armored [[Resistance trooper|troopers]] like its predecessor. The First Order had its own version of the [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtrooper]].<ref name="TFA VD">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> Meanwhile, the [[Sith Eternal]] cult had raised an [[Sith Eternal army|army]]<ref name="SWCEUAE">''[[Star Wars: Character Encyclopedia, Updated and Expanded Edition]]''</ref> in secret,<ref name="Episode IX">{{Film|IX}}</ref> whose most elite soldiers were the crimson-armored [[Sith trooper]]s.<ref name="Secrets of the Sith">''[[Star Wars: The Secrets of the Sith]]''</ref> Legions of Sith troopers were prepared<ref name="TROS VD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> for the final conquest of the galaxy, but the Sith Eternal was ultimately destroyed in the [[Battle of Exegol]]. The First Order then saw [[Uprising against the First Order|uprisings against its military]] across the galaxy.<ref name="Episode IX" />

